  correct_choice_id = $q$a$q$,
  rationale = $q$When responding to auditory hallucinations, the nurse should: (1) Validate the client's reality and feeling while stating the nurse's reality ('I do not hear any voices, but I see that you are frightened'), and (2) Immediately assess for COMMAND hallucinations ('What are the voices telling you to do?'). Command hallucinations instructing self-harm or violence represent a psychiatric emergency. The nurse must never validate the hallucination as real (Option D), brgue or mock the client (Option B), or give advice to talk to the voices (Option C).$q$
