-- twelve worst it ran 1.82 to 1.97 times the longest distractor, which lets a candidate score
-- without knowing the medicine.
-- 
-- Two moves per item, and neither changes the correct answer. First, the keyed option is cut back
-- to the action it states - the trailing explanation it carried belongs in the rationale, and the
-- rationale already carried it. Second, the distractors are extended so that each states the
-- mechanism it presumes instead of a bare phrase, which is the same standard the length gate
-- applied to the ratio outliers.
-- 
-- Items: NG-LAB-0156, NG-ANP-0090, NG-BUS-0713, NG-ORIGINAL-NCX-0011, NG-ORIGINAL-NCX-0024,
-- NG-ORIGINAL-NCX-0027, NG-ORIGINAL-NCX-0156, NG-ORIGINAL-NCX-0247, NG-ORIGINAL-NCX-0271,
-- NG-ORIGINAL-NCX-0604, NG-ORIGINAL-NCX-0132, NG-ORIGINAL-NCX-0862.
-- 
-- Every key keeps its letter. The rationale quote is updated wherever it repeats the keyed option,
-- so CORRECT (X) - "..." still matches the option word for word. No keyed option in these twelve is
-- the longest any more; the ratios now run 0.85 to 0.98.
-- 
-- Bank-wide the length gate is unchanged, worst 2.00 and nothing above it, and key balance is
